From 7205f37a47d9216c8264cf71369d8ad2e13a5fae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alpha10-1 <92021278+Alpha10-1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:36:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: capacity/allocation tracking for staff assignments

Adds planned % allocation to individual project assignments and a
firm-wide capacity dashboard, so over/under-staffing is visible before
new work gets assigned.

Backend:
- ProjectAssignment.allocation_percent (1-100, nullable): planned % of
  a person's time committed to the engagement. Only valid on individual
  (user_id) assignments -- a department assignment staffs the whole team
  without a per-person split, so it's rejected there (422) rather than
  silently ignored.
- PUT /projects/{project_id}/assignments/{assignment_id}: update role
  and/or allocation_percent on an existing assignment.
- GET /reports/dashboard/capacity: for every active (non-disabled) staff
  member, sums allocation_percent across open (planning/active/on_hold)
  engagements and buckets them as over_allocated (>100%), under_allocated
  (<50%), fully_allocated, or bench (no assignments). Tracks assignments
  with no allocation_percent set separately rather than silently treating
  them as 0% or 100%.
- Migration b2d3e4f5a6b7. Verified against the actual pre-migration
  schema (reconstructed from git history, stamped at the prior revision,
  then upgraded with the new code) rather than a synthetic test -- clean
  upgrade, correct resulting schema.
- 11 new tests, 188 total passing.

Frontend:
- projects/page.js (Team tab): allocation-% input when assigning an
  individual, inline-editable % on existing individual assignments.
- reports/page.js: new Capacity tab alongside Per-Partner/Per-Client/
  Compliance -- over/under-allocated/bench counts and a per-person
  breakdown with their engagements.
- src/lib/api.js: updateProjectAssignment, fetchCapacityDashboard.
- Verified with esbuild JSX syntax check and a full 'next build' (clean).
